WEBVTT

NOTE Draft cue timing follows measured scene audio and word count. Review spoken word alignment before publication.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.087
Welcome to Resgrid Academy. In this lesson, we will give members a dependable

00:00:05.087 --> 00:00:10.174
reference library. Procedures and contacts hidden in individual email threads are difficult to

00:00:10.174 --> 00:00:15.261
find and keep current. We will explain the features, the setup decisions, and

00:00:15.261 --> 00:00:18.000
a practical way to check the result.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:24.080
A department uploads its standard operating procedures, adds hospital and mutual-aid contacts and

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:29.561
creates a medical dispatch protocol. Members find the current procedure, preplan or phone

00:00:29.561 --> 00:00:35.041
number when they need it instead of searching email. The examples in this

00:00:35.041 --> 00:00:40.100
series use a fictional department and are teaching scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:47.322
Contacts. Shared contacts such as hospitals, agencies and vendors. Add the outside contacts

00:00:47.322 --> 00:00:48.850
members call most.

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:55.825
Documents. Shared documents such as procedures and preplans. Upload your most-used documents and

00:00:55.825 --> 00:01:02.199
organize them by category. Availability also depends on Documents. Check access in the

00:01:02.199 --> 00:01:03.180
target department.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:10.323
Protocols. Dispatch protocols with scripted questions and instructions. Create protocols for the call

00:01:10.323 --> 00:01:12.840
types that need scripted questions.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:18.947
New Contact. Add a person or organization contact. Gather the documents and contacts

00:01:18.947 --> 00:01:22.760
members need most, and decide who keeps them current.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:29.814
Contact Categories. Categories for organizing contacts. Gather the documents and contacts members need

00:01:29.814 --> 00:01:33.290
most, and decide who keeps them current.

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:39.809
Upload Document. Upload a document. Gather the documents and contacts members need most,

00:01:39.809 --> 00:01:45.729
and decide who keeps them current. Availability also depends on Documents. Check access

00:01:45.729 --> 00:01:47.550
in the target department.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:53.708
Notes. Short shared notes for the department. Gather the documents and contacts members

00:01:53.708 --> 00:01:59.265
need most, and decide who keeps them current. Availability also depends on Notes.

00:01:59.265 --> 00:02:01.830
Check access in the target department.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:07.932
New Note. Post a department note. Gather the documents and contacts members need

00:02:07.932 --> 00:02:13.434
most, and decide who keeps them current. Availability also depends on Notes. Check

00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:15.550
access in the target department.

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:21.831
New Protocol. Create a dispatch protocol. Gather the documents and contacts members need

00:02:21.831 --> 00:02:24.890
most, and decide who keeps them current.

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:31.003
Forms. Custom forms used on calls and dispatches. Gather the documents and contacts

00:02:31.003 --> 00:02:34.820
members need most, and decide who keeps them current.

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:40.880
Shared links. Share selected calls, units and personnel with a linked department. Gather

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:46.340
the documents and contacts members need most, and decide who keeps them current.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:52.866
Files and attachments. Files attached to documents and records. Gather the documents and

00:02:52.866 --> 00:02:58.793
contacts members need most, and decide who keeps them current. Availability also depends

00:02:58.793 --> 00:03:02.440
on Documents. Check access in the target department.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:08.941
Connect provides a department profile, posts, and communication surfaces. Review the intended public

00:03:08.941 --> 00:03:14.842
profile content, then prepare a fictional profile and sample post through their owning

00:03:14.842 --> 00:03:20.743
screens. Check the visible audience and the published sample content in the demo

00:03:20.743 --> 00:03:26.190
environment. Confirm availability in the demo department before recording the live workflow.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:32.148
Navigation search helps members find the work they are authorized to access. Search

00:03:32.148 --> 00:03:37.505
for a known department feature using a member account and an administrator account.

00:03:37.505 --> 00:03:42.863
Compare the returned navigation options with each account permission scope. Confirm availability in

00:03:42.863 --> 00:03:46.160
the demo department before recording the live workflow.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:52.551
For the training scenario, work in this order. Step 1. Add key outside

00:03:52.551 --> 00:03:58.342
contacts and organize categories. Step 2. Upload a current procedure and set its

00:03:58.342 --> 00:04:04.134
intended visibility. Step 3. Create approved protocol questions or a form for a

00:04:04.134 --> 00:04:05.470
repeatable dispatch task.

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:12.670
Now verify the result. Open the contact, document, protocol, and form as an

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:19.270
intended member. Check ownership, version currency, attachments, and visibility. A common problem to

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:25.869
watch for: A shared link needs an explicit data-sharing review. Keep protocol content

00:04:25.869 --> 00:04:27.900
aligned with department-approved procedures.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:33.575
Your practice task is simple. Find the hospital contact and current procedure as

00:04:33.575 --> 00:04:38.651
a sample member. Track outdated material and items without a responsible owner. Record

00:04:38.651 --> 00:04:43.726
the result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed. Use

00:04:43.726 --> 00:04:47.630
the linked feature scripts for the detailed screen recording plan.

